# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

WHILE game is running

    Display current room

    Prompt player:
    "Enter your move (North, South, East, West)"

    Input direction

    IF direction is a valid exit from the current room THEN

        Move player to the new room

        Display:
        "You moved to [new room]"

    ELSE

        Display:
        "You can't go that way."

    END IF

END WHILE
IF direction == "North" AND North exit exists
    Move to northern room

ELSE IF direction == "South" AND South exit exists
    Move to southern room

ELSE IF direction == "East" AND East exit exists
    Move to eastern room

ELSE IF direction == "West" AND West exit exists
    Move to western room

ELSE
    Display "Invalid direction."
END IF


